From: OpenWrt EcoNet port
Subject: watchdog: airoha: allow building on the EcoNet MIPS SoCs

The EN751627 carries the same watchdog block as the EN7581 -- timer3 of
the legacy timer unit at 0x1fbf0100, identical register layout -- but
the driver is gated on ARCH_AIROHA, which only covers the ARM64 side of
the family. The MIPS EcoNet SoCs are the same lineage (they already
share the airoha gpio, scu, snand and uart drivers), so widen the
dependency rather than duplicating the driver.

--- a/drivers/watchdog/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/Kconfig
@@ -422,7 +422,7 @@
 
 config AIROHA_WATCHDOG
 	tristate "Airoha EN7581 Watchdog"
-	depends on ARCH_AIROHA || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on ARCH_AIROHA || ECONET || COMPILE_TEST
 	select WATCHDOG_CORE
 	help
 	  Watchdog timer embedded into Airoha SoC. This will reboot your
